{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KHJf52xcBXfKasYMRjip74","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development. It derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go binaries, `pkg/` holds shared libraries (sys, format, testutils), `magefiles/` drives orchestration, `docs/` holds specs.\n\n**Current state:** Releases 00.0 through 05.3 have been implemented. Release 05.4 (checksum quartet: md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) is the current target. Recent commits (task 365) already implemented the `cmd/` binaries for all four checksum utilities. Tests remain.\n\n**Current release:** 05.4 — all four use cases (md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum) have spec_complete status. Implementation binaries were committed in task 365; differential tests are the remaining work.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe checksum quartet shares an identical interface: read files or stdin, compute hash, output `<hash>  <filename>`. All four can share a test pattern. Since task 365 already created the `cmd/` binaries, the next task is differential tests. All four test files fit within the 250-line budget because checksum tests are structurally identical (same flags: `-c`, `-b`, `--check`, `--status`, `--warn`, `--strict`, `--quiet`, `--tag`; same stdin/file input patterns).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Task 367: Differential tests for checksum quartet cmd/ binaries (rel05.4-uc001 md5sum, rel05.4-uc002 sha1sum, rel05.4-uc003 sha256sum, rel05.4-uc004 sha512sum)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-05.4.yaml (test cases for all four checksum utilities)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (PRDs for md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum -- locate by name)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml (use case for md5sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc002-sha1sum.yaml (use case for sha1sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc003-sha256sum.yaml (use case for sha256sum)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc004-sha512sum.yaml (use case for sha512sum)\n      - cmd/md5sum/main.go (existing implementation from prior task)\n      - cmd/sha1sum/main.go (existing implementation from prior task)\n      - cmd/sha256sum/main.go (existing implementation from prior task)\n      - cmd/sha512sum/main.go (existing implementation from prior task)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness API)\n      - cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go (reference for differential test pattern in a recent utility)\n      - cmd/comm/comm_test.go (reference for differential test pattern in a recent utility)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for md5sum against gmd5sum reference binary\n      - path: cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for sha1sum against gsha1sum reference binary\n      - path: cmd/sha256sum/sha256sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for sha256sum against gsha256sum reference binary\n      - path: cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for sha512sum against gsha512sum reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement differential tests for cmd/md5sum covering: basic file hashing,\n          stdin hashing, multiple file arguments, -c/--check mode (valid and corrupt\n          checksums), --tag (BSD-style output), -b/--binary flag, and missing file\n          error handling. Use testutils.BuildBinary and testutils.RunDiffTests.\n          Reference binary is \"gmd5sum\" via exec.LookPath.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement differential tests for cmd/sha1sum with the same test case\n          categories as R1. Reference binary is \"gsha1sum\" via exec.LookPath.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement differential tests for cmd/sha256sum with the same test case\n          categories as R1. Reference binary is \"gsha256sum\" via exec.LookPath.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Implement differential tests for cmd/sha512sum with the same test case\n          categories as R1. Reference binary is \"gsha512sum\" via exec.LookPath.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Follow the established differential test pattern from other cmd/ packages.\n          Each test file has a single TestDiff function that builds the Go binary\n          with testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\"), looks up the reference binary with\n          exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\"), calls t.Skip if the reference is not found,\n          defines a []testutils.DiffTest slice, and calls testutils.RunDiffTests.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          For --check mode tests, create temporary checksum files in t.TempDir().\n          Generate the checksum file by running the Go binary on a known input file,\n          then use -c against the generated checksum file. Also test a corrupted\n          checksum file (modified hash) to verify error output and exit code.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          All four test files share the same structure and test categories because\n          the utilities have identical CLI interfaces (only the hash algorithm\n          differs). Read existing cmd/ test files (e.g., cmd/uniq/uniq_test.go,\n          cmd/comm/comm_test.go) to match the project's established style and\n          patterns exactly.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Set LC_ALL=C in the Env field of every DiffTest to match the project\n          convention for deterministic output comparison.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go exists and go test ./cmd/md5sum/ passes\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go exists and go test ./cmd/sha1sum/ passes\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"cmd/sha256sum/sha256sum_test.go exists and go test ./cmd/sha256sum/ passes\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go exists and go test ./cmd/sha512sum/ passes\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Each test file includes at least: basic file hash, stdin hash, multiple files, --check with valid file, --check with corrupt file, --tag output, and missing file error case\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/md5sum/ ./cmd/sha1sum/ ./cmd/sha256sum/ ./cmd/sha512sum/ reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27585,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27585},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"659a3658-92fa-4261-a2fa-7b7edf7b4cbb","uuid":"d7216ff0-76ce-4bd9-9edf-09d0bd515703"}
